in Mexico this morning a major city is  under lockdown after Security Forces  arrested the son of the drug kingpin  Joaquin El Chapo Guzman yesterday the  arrest led to an explosion of violence  in culiacan at least seven members of  the security forces were killed the  alleged drug cartel leader is now in  custody in Mexico City as Errol Barnett  reports this is not the first time the  younger Guzman has been arrested  the arrest of ovideo Guzman triggered a  violent response in culiacan Mexico home  base to the Sinaloa drug cartel armed  groups torch cars buses and trucks the  son of the notorious drug lord Joaquin  El Chapo Guzman was captured in a dawn  raid in the city after months of  surveillance  Mexico's defense secretary says security  stopped a vehicle carrying the suspected  drug trafficker once they nabbed Guzman  he says they came under heavy fire and  despite the barriers set up around kulia  Khan the Air Force was able to fly  Guzman to Mexico City  however the airport in kulia Khan came  under heavy fire during the operation  gunmen shooting at this Air Force plane  on the runway bullets hitting this Aero  Mexico flight while on the tarmac  sending passengers to take cover no one  was injured Thursday's arrest marks a  dramatic turn from the last time Guzman  was apprehended in the same city back in  2019 then after the titanium Guzman's  security and cartel members engaged in a  lethal day of violence only for  authorities to later release him Guzman  now faces charges in the U.S where his  father is serving a life sentence and a  Maximum Security federal prison in  Colorado it is not yet clear if  prosecutors have requested extradition  for the younger Guzman CBS mornings I'm  Errol Barnett
 

